markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Section 3: Python Basics</h1>

<div style="display: inline-block; background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold; font-size: 13px; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 12px;">Aligns to curriculum Lessons 3-5</div>

<p>This section prepares you to teach three curriculum lessons. Once students have a working definition of intelligence and a sense of AI's history, Section 3 shifts into the technical foundation everything else in the unit depends on: actual Python syntax.</p>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><b>Curriculum Lesson 3:</b> Algorithms</div>
  <a href="PASTE_AIF_Y2_UNIT_1_LESSON_3_URL_HERE" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 3</a>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><b>Curriculum Lesson 4:</b> Hello, AI</div>
  <a href="PASTE_AIF_Y2_UNIT_1_LESSON_4_URL_HERE" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 4</a>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><b>Curriculum Lesson 5:</b> Defining Functions</div>
  <a href="PASTE_AIF_Y2_UNIT_1_LESSON_5_URL_HERE" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 5</a>
</div>

<hr>

<p><b>In this section, you'll:</b></p>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Translate a plain-language instruction into pseudocode, then into working Python, the same translation step students will practice repeatedly</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Read and write variables as a way of storing and updating information a program needs as it runs</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Define a function and call it, and get clear yourself on the difference before you have to explain it under pressure</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Practice reading a Python error message for what it's actually telling you, rather than treating it as a dead end</div>
<div style="font-size: 16px;">&bull; See where this foundation gets used immediately: hill climbing in curriculum Lesson 6, loops in curriculum Lessons 7-8</div>

<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222; line-height: 1.5;"><b>&#128161; Notice as you explore:</b> how "defining" a function and "calling" it are two separate actions that even experienced programmers moving between languages mix up sometimes. Expect to revisit this distinction more than once, it rarely clicks the first time it's explained.</div>
</div>

<hr>

<div style="display: flex; gap: 6px; margin-top: 24px; max-width: 700px;">
  <div style="flex: 1; text-align: center; background-color: #ACA8EA; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; font-size: 13px; padding: 10px 4px; border-radius: 6px;">Section 1</div>
